From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Golmann <684458+pjeweb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:34:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 55/57] thermal: expose the device-tree node of OF cooling devices

Expose device-tree identity so userspace can correlate thermal cooling
state with readings from the same physical device through hwmon or other
subsystems. The driver core emits an of_node link and OF_* uevent
variables for every OF cooling device, including CPU and devfreq cooling
devices. Document both as userspace ABI.

First-party: authored by CeraLive against v7.2, with no upstream
counterpart in rockchip-rk3588-mainline-patches. The source of record
is ceralive/0055-thermal-cooling-device-of-node.patch
and patches/ is generated from it by scripts/build-series.py.
scripts/verify-payload-parity.py holds it to the same
added/removed-line parity the upstream lane gets.

Intended for upstream review on linux-pm.
Submission and DCO sign-off are separate from this integration.

---
diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-class-thermal b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-class-thermal
index 968d89e..de6cb0d 100644
--- a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-class-thermal
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-class-thermal
@@ -223,6 +223,27 @@ Description:
 
 		RW, Required
 
+What:		/sys/class/thermal/cooling_deviceX/of_node
+Date:		November 2026
+Contact:	linux-pm@vger.kernel.org
+Description:
+		Symbolic link to the device tree node associated with this
+		cooling device. This allows userspace to find other kernel
+		interfaces for the same device by comparing their of_node links.
+
+		Present for cooling devices registered with a device tree node.
+
+What:		/sys/class/thermal/cooling_deviceX/uevent
+Date:		November 2026
+Contact:	linux-pm@vger.kernel.org
+Description:
+		For cooling devices registered with a device tree node, the
+		standard OF_* variables describe that node. OF_NAME and
+		OF_FULLNAME identify it. OF_TYPE, OF_COMPATIBLE_* and
+		OF_ALIAS_* describe the information available in the tree.
+		The same variables are included in the corresponding device
+		uevents.
+
 What:		/sys/class/thermal/cooling_deviceX/stats/reset
 Description:
 		Writing any value resets the cooling device's statistics.
diff --git a/drivers/thermal/thermal_core.c b/drivers/thermal/thermal_core.c
index 28a20d4..53a8391 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/thermal_core.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/thermal_core.c
@@ -958,6 +958,7 @@ static void thermal_cdev_release(struct device *dev)
 	struct thermal_cooling_device *cdev = to_cooling_device(dev);
 
 	thermal_cooling_device_destroy_sysfs(cdev);
+	of_node_put(dev->of_node);
 	kfree_const(cdev->type);
 	ida_free(&thermal_cdev_ida, cdev->id);
 	kfree(cdev);
@@ -1013,6 +1014,8 @@ int thermal_cooling_device_add(struct thermal_cooling_device *cdev, void *devdat
 	cdev->device.class = thermal_class;
 	cdev->device.release = thermal_cdev_release;
 	device_initialize(&cdev->device);
+	/* Expose the DT identity alongside the cooling state in sysfs. */
+	cdev->device.of_node = of_node_get(cdev->np);
 	cdev->devdata = devdata;
 
 	ret = dev_set_name(&cdev->device, "cooling_device%d", cdev->id);
